================================================================================
DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SettingsPage shipped at parity with the web /settings page: a pure
@Observable SettingsPageModel (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the page's 12 web i18n keys,
the load state driven by an injectable SettingsPageDataSource (web useSettings/GET /settings — success AND
failure resolve to the rendered content, faithful to the web PageContainer loading-only gate), the
edit-conflict visibility (web EditConflictBanner/useEditLease), and real, faithful tour/checklist actions
over injectable seams (NotificationTourLauncher posts the web 'teslasync:tour:openLauncher' event;
UserDefaultsSettingsChecklistStore clears the web checklist localStorage keys + posts the web
'teslasync:checklist:changed' event + surfaces the restarted confirmation — web restartChecklist + toast).
The view reproduces every region of the manifest's scope — the header (title + subtitle), the edit-conflict
banner, and the three action GlassPanels (Data Export link → .exports via the shell onNavigate; Onboarding
Tour; Setup Checklist with its inline success confirmation) — with the web loading→content gate (centered
spinner → panels). A dedicated `.settingsPage` route (pathSegment settings/overview, .account group) +
`/settings` & `/settings/overview` parser aliases + registration make it sidebar-reachable and
`/settings` deep-linkable, while leaving the pre-existing native `.settings`/AppSettingsView preferences
surface fully intact (reachable via /account + the ⌘, scene; RouteTests invariants preserved). Verified on
BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0, incl. previews) + the
executed model & route harness (34/34) + the shimmed XCTest type-check + swiftformat/swiftlint --strict
(0/0) + the placeholder scan (0). The full xcodebuild scheme was NOT run — it is gated on the out-of-scope,
P1-owned KMP `Shared.xcframework` Gradle staging (the app module imports `Shared`; staging OOM-kills this
shared parallel-slot host per the sibling logs), and triggering it would be irresponsible on a shared
runner; deferred to its owner / the P99 integration gate.

